The Timothy Loveridge writes:
-=> 	  I have been trying to compile NETHACK 3.0 with NDMAKE 4.3.  It works
-=> fine upto a point, then out of the blue it says: Out of memory. Stop.  It
-=> should have plenty of memory, I have 640 K of RAM and still have 54 K left
-=> during the compiles most of the time.  Even when I compile all of the
-=> files seperately, it says Out of Memory.

A tip from the latest Install.dos:  Try 'make -n >>compile.bat', then
enter 'compile'.  You'll avoid NDMAKE's overhead entirely.  The link
command will be too long for MS-DOS to execute, so you'll have to 'make'
that separately.


